//////////////////
CameraManager controls which camera is active.
Camera sets position and look at into CameraManager.
Render creates the View-Projection matrix.
Renderables Base have a Transform that stores their position, rotation, scale.
Renderables Base have a PreRender() function that gets passed a reference to a structure that contains the VP matrix.
Renderables PreRender() set the MVP in the shader.
Renderables derived then have Render called, where the actual draw calls are made.

How to manage application-specific cameras? How to add a camera from outside Core?
Maybe be able to register a camera with CameraManager, get back an id. 

