TextureManager has CreateTexture calls that load images, bind the textures.
MaterialManager optionally allows inclusion of a texture name. If a material is assigned a texture, it gets the uniform "mainTex".

How will textures be referenced? Will each asset have a UID assigned, then scene hierarchy uses that reference.
TextureManager can load all textures found in a folder, than the app can reference by name. Requires unique name, which won't work if multiple models use the same naming convention in their materials.
Unity has an asset database that provides darg and drop to connect assets. For now, assets will be connected by name, a string assigned, like materials.

Transform class with position, rotation, scale.
SceneObject class has-a Transform.
Renderable derived from SceneObject, MVP set from SceneObject values.
References to instances of Classes derived from Renderable or SceneObject can access Transform to set position, rotation, scale.

Should Renderables be-a SceneObject, or should SceneObject have-a Renderable?
Should SceneObjects determine update order as well as render order? Render order can use scene hierarch for visibility culling, then drawing front to back. However, cpu-side update order does not need to be the same as render order. Update ordder should follow hierarchical state machine.

