Tasks:
* MeshRenderable takes verts, incidices and maybe normals. Quad, Cube, then Sphere can derive from that.
* RenderablePrimitive will have an enum of types: cube, sphere, line, axis. It will hold the verts etc for each type.

Every mesh must have:
* vertices
* uvs
* indices
Required for lighting:
* normals

Rendering options:
* Lit or Unlit
* Textured or not
* Coloured or not


```
+----------------+-----+----------+----------+
| Type           | Lit | Textured | Coloured |
+----------------+-----+----------+----------+
| Mesh           |  X  |    X     |    X     |
| Primitive      |  X  |          |    X     |
| Procedural     |     |          |          |
| Particle, UI   |     |    X     |    X     |
+----------------+-----+----------+----------+
```
Shaders:
LitTextured: expects normals, model, lights, uvs, texture
LitColoured: expects normals, model, lights, no uvs, texture
UnlitTextured: expects uvs, texture, no normals
Procedural: expects uvs, time, aspect ratio

Material creation and update:
Material will have uniforms set during init that must match the shader, and adds them to its list of uniforms found on the shader. Assert the correct uniforms are found.

When renderable calls it's Render(), SetUniform() checks the uniform map if the 

