Input Action Management:
Game code uses InputActions, a context-specific name, either enum or text label.
InputActions map to InputTriggers. These are gamepad-specific inputs, or debug keyboard input. This enforces a gamepad-oriented control scheme.
InputTriggers map to keyboard combos or gamepad input.
InputActions can have multiple maps or contexts, so depending on the situation, different sets of InputActions can be used.

