Design a UI layout and styling system that has an html-and-css-like format. It will support a common subset of UI elements, some of which are interactable. Interaction can b triggerred by mouse or touch click, or by triggering the 'selected' element, which infers a non-mouse navigation system that can be manipulated via keys or gamepad. Interactable elements have state of enabled, disabled, selected/hovered. Support a slice-9 image and a way to define the image sections for that. Elements: panel (the container of other elements, always a root panel, optional background), button, font text, slider, switch toggles, dropdowns. Requires a high-quality text/font rendering system, which can be added first as a separate task if that makes sense.
The UI layer will be a fullscreen quad blitted on top of the 3D scene after post-processing has been applied: 3D scene -> post effects -> UI.
We will eventually create a UI Layout and Stying Design and Tech markdown doc in the planning folder after we iterate on the design.

